WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.940 line:17%
Families may feel shock or denial when a diagnosis

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:03.840 line:17%
is unexpected.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:08.280 line:17%
Anger, fear, bargaining, and sadness can also appear as

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:08.920 line:17%
they adjust.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.720 line:17%
Imagine a family that has settled into a routine

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:12.860 line:17%
with hearing technology.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:16.530 line:17%
When a new school makes communication harder, some of

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:17.810 line:17%
the earlier worry returns.

00:00:18.552 --> 00:00:20.870 line:17%
That change is compatible with healthy adjustment.

00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.660 line:17%
The stages describe possible reactions, and families can move

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.300 line:17%
back and forth over time.

00:00:27.631 --> 00:00:30.491 line:17%
When a caregiver says they feel overwhelmed, give that

00:00:30.491 --> 00:00:31.131 line:17%
feeling room.

00:00:31.883 --> 00:00:34.531 line:17%
Telling them to stop worrying can close the conversation

00:00:34.531 --> 00:00:35.771 line:17%
before you know what is hard.

00:00:36.631 --> 00:00:39.491 line:17%
Try reflecting the concern, then ask what would make

00:00:39.491 --> 00:00:40.751 line:17%
the next step manageable.

00:00:41.531 --> 00:00:44.351 line:17%
A support group, clear information, or a chance to

00:00:44.351 --> 00:00:46.291 line:17%
practice with the device can build confidence.

00:00:47.322 --> 00:00:49.751 line:17%
A clinician can offer support and connect the family

00:00:49.751 --> 00:00:51.971 line:17%
with a mental health professional when their needs go

00:00:51.971 --> 00:00:53.411 line:17%
beyond audiologic counseling.
